// The shape-dependent half of the bench harness (issue #191): the pinned
// instance, the LCG vary mapping, and — where the leg has no free memory
// barrier — the §2.7 full-struct sink fold and the decoded-field check.
//
// The pin is the wire golden itself, decoded: testdata/wire/<shape>.bin is
// the §1.5 oracle every leg is gated against, so it is the ONE source of
// the pinned values and no leg transcribes them.
//
// The vary mapping is derived from each field's declared wire type: a
// masked draw of the largest power-of-two sub-range inside the field's
// bounds, offset by its minimum, from one LCG word (§2.2). Structure —
// array counts, string and bytes used lengths, the union tag, a branch
// gate — never varies, so bytes/op is constant (§2.7). Array elements vary
// at stride 2 through their value fields, the family's representative
// subset made mechanical.
//
